@startuml "Facade - Compiler - Class Diagram"
skinparam classAttributeIconSize 0
hide empty members
title Facade — GoF's own compiler subsystem


class Client
class Compiler <<Facade>> {
  + compile(source) : BytecodeStream
  + compile(source, generator)
}

package "compiler subsystem" {
  class Scanner
  class Parser
  class ProgramNodeBuilder
  class ProgramNode
  abstract class CodeGenerator
  class StackMachineCodeGenerator
  class RiscCodeGenerator
  class BytecodeStream
}

Client --> Compiler
Compiler ..> Scanner
Compiler ..> Parser
Compiler ..> ProgramNodeBuilder
Compiler ..> CodeGenerator
CodeGenerator <|-- StackMachineCodeGenerator
CodeGenerator <|-- RiscCodeGenerator

note right of Compiler
  Two public methods over
  eight subsystem classes.
end note

note bottom of Scanner
  The subsystem knows <b>nothing</b>
  about the facade. A facade
  depends on its subsystem,
  never the reverse.
end note

note as N1
  GoF, p. 185: a facade "doesn't prevent
  applications from using subsystem classes
  if they need to."

  A front door, <b>not a wall</b>.
end note

@enduml
